.TH ZVM-ALIAS 1 "August 2026" "ZVM" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-alias \- name installed Zig versions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm alias
.br
.B zvm alias
.I name
.br
.B zvm alias
.I name version
.br
.B zvm alias
.BR --delete " " name
.br
.B zvm alias --clear
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create, inspect, list, or delete aliases for installed Zig versions.
.B kv
is an alias for the
.B alias
command.
.PP
With no arguments, list every alias.
With only
.IR name ,
print that alias.
With
.I name
and
.IR version ,
create or replace an alias.
The target version must already be installed; version shorthand is accepted.
.PP
Aliases may be used as version arguments to
.BR install ,
.BR use ,
.BR run ,
and
.BR uninstall .
They are stored in
.I aliases.json
under the ZVM base directory, as a JSON object of name to version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -d , " " --delete
Delete the named alias.
Deleting an alias that does not exist succeeds.
.TP
.B --clear
Delete all aliases.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zvm alias work 0.14.1
zvm kv play .13
zvm alias work
zvm alias
zvm alias --delete work
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.zvm/aliases.json
Alias file.
If
.B ZVM_PATH
is set, the file is
.IR $ZVM_PATH/aliases.json .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-use (1),
.BR zvm-run (1),
.BR zvm-uninstall (1)
